# SHEYTAN-Local-Agent — build & runtime artifacts
# Source is Go; everything below is generated at build or run time.
#
# ⚠ v1.0.11 LESSON — KEEP THE LEADING SLASHES:
# Runtime data dirs are created NEXT TO THE EXE (repo root in dev). The
# leading "/" anchors them to the repo root ONLY. Without it, the unanchored
# `sessions/` and `sandbox/` patterns ALSO matched internal/sessions/ and
# internal/sandbox/ — the two packages silently never got committed, which
# is exactly what broke the v1.0.9 and v1.0.10 CI builds. A regression test
# (internal/releasegate) now fails the build if a pattern swallows source.
# The same gate runs in GitHub Actions via `go test ./internal/...`.

# Build outputs
/dist-stage/
/build/
*.exe
*.syso
*.zip
/local-agent
/build.log
/build1.log

# Runtime data (portable app creates these next to the exe — repo root only)
/models/
/workspace/
/charts/
/sessions/
/logs/
/browser-profile/
/sandbox/
/data/
/config.json
/installed.json

# Test-generated artifacts land under /build/ (covered above).

# Go tooling
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Vite build output (synced into web/static at build time)
/dist/

# Node frontend dependencies (npm install — root only, never commit)
/node_modules/

# Go module cache/proxies pulled by local tooling
/vendor/
